<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('../../partials/head') %>
  <%# UX fix (owner, 2026-09-06: "show each profile as a card and the action
       buttons have to sticky at the top. If there are 100 profiles, it is
       not desirable to scroll all the way down") — .profile-tile is
       .card-tile (CR-083's own card family: crisp border, hover accent)
       plus a persistent "selected" highlight once its checkbox is checked,
       not just on hover. Page-only enhancement, doesn't touch any shared
       CR-083 rule. %>
  <style>
    .profile-tile:has(input:checked) {
      border-color: var(--primary-dark) !important;
      background: var(--primary-light);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header><%- include('../../partials/navbar') %></header>

  <% var wide = locals.fromObjective && fromObjective.commissioningOptions && fromObjective.commissioningOptions.length && !fromObjective.commissionedSeuId; %>
  <main class="container py-5" style="max-width: <%= wide ? '1100px' : '700px' %>;">
    <% if (locals.flash) { %>
      <div class="alert alert-<%= flash.type === 'error' ? 'danger' : 'success' %> alert-dismissible fade show border-0 shadow-sm mb-4" role="alert">
        <i class="bi bi-<%= flash.type === 'error' ? 'exclamation-triangle' : 'check-circle' %> me-2"></i><%= flash.message %>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="alert"></button>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <% if (locals.fromObjective) { %>
      <%# Bug fix (owner: "The commission SEU should get onto the SEU screen
           and the messages has to be on that screen. Not on the objective
           screen.") — commissioning against an existing Objective now lands
           here instead of being decided inline on the Objective's own detail
           page.
           Redesigned (owner, 2026-09-05: "Objectives only propose
           capabilities. They do not take the final call... capability-name
           -> templates -> profile And allow the user to choose a profile. If
           an additional capability is required, profiles have provision for
           that.") — no more auto-matched single Template/hard failure;
           fromObjective.commissioningOptions (getObjectiveDetail,
           core/objectives.ts) is browsed and picked here rather than
           computed.
           Inverted (owner, 2026-09-06: "The whole selection of
           template+profile is messed up. It has to be inverted. Show the
           list of all applicable profiles first - which template they
           correspond to and the capability name as a list... no
           duplication of profiles") — one row per real Profile (never
           repeated even when its Template covers several required
           Capabilities), each row naming its own Template and listing
           every required Capability that Template covers. A Template with
           no real Profile yet ("template + no profile - i agree with your
           approach") gets its own single row instead (profile: null, "a
           default will be created"). A chosen Template missing something
           else the Objective proposed isn't a blocker — its Profile's own
           Additional Capabilities (Ch.7 §5) is where that gets covered, not
           here. %>
      <h2 class="h3 mb-1 text-dark fw-bold">Commission SEU from Objective</h2>
      <p class="mb-4"><%= fromObjective.objective.statement %></p>

      <%# Bug fix (owner, 2026-09-06: "The corresponding objective should not
           allow any more commissioning requests against the same
           objective") — a direct/stale link to this Objective (e.g. from a
           bookmark, or before a tree row's own "Commissioned" badge
           refreshes) must not fall through to the generic "no Template
           available" message below — that reads as a Template gap, not as
           "already done." %>
      <% if (fromObjective.commissionedSeuId) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-success mb-0">
          This Objective has already been commissioned. <a href="/aisworg/seu/seus/<%= fromObjective.commissionedSeuId %>">View the SEU</a>.
        </div>
      <% } else if (!fromObjective.commissioningOptions || !fromObjective.commissioningOptions.length) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-warning mb-0">No Template is currently available to commission against.</div>
      <% } else { %>
        <%# Redesigned (owner, 2026-09-06: "Multiple profiles are very much
             possible. That is why composition exists. That is why
             validation is required... choose one or more profiles. And has
             to queue to validate") — was a single radio (one Template +
             Profile pair); now checkboxes, one-or-more selections, posted to
             validate-commission (not directly to commission) so every
             selection passes through a real conflict check first. %>
        <%# CR-083 (Modern Light Theme & Crisp UI Boundary Overhaul) — this
             picker previously used plain Bootstrap card/shadow/list-group
             utility classes, matching this file's own pre-CR-083 pattern
             rather than the app's own .section-card/.section-header/
             .component-row design-system classes (public/css/style.css)
             every sibling SEU-area page (e.g. objectives/detail.ejs) is
             built from. Aligned now.
             UX fix (owner, 2026-09-06: "show each profile as a card and
             the action buttons have to sticky at the top. If there are
             100 profiles, it is not desirable to scroll all the way
             down") — rows became a card grid (.card-tile, same
             CR-083-governed card family, one Profile per card), and the
             submit/cancel actions moved out of a footer below however
             many cards there are into their own toolbar, sticky at the
             top of the viewport as the grid scrolls underneath it.
             Bug fix (owner, 2026-09-06: "Let us impose the condition that
             only one profile can be chosen. Now it is a multi-select") —
             CR-092 Part 6's own "allow multiple Profiles" policy is
             retired; back to a single choice — checkboxes reverted to a
             radio group (same shared name="templateProfile" already
             enforced mutual exclusivity for a radio, no other markup
             change needed). commissionSeu's own guard
             (core/commissioning.ts) is the real backstop; this is just the
             form matching that rule. %>
        <form method="POST" action="/aisworg/seu/objectives/<%= fromObjective.objective.id %>/validate-commission">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <div class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between gap-3 mb-3" style="position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); padding: .85rem 1.25rem;">
            <span class="small text-muted">Choose one Profile below, then Queue to Validate.</span>
            <div class="d-flex gap-2 flex-shrink-0">
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm"><i class="bi bi-clipboard-check me-1"></i>Queue to Validate</button>
              <a href="/aisworg/seu/objectives/<%= fromObjective.objective.id %>" class="btn btn-link text-muted btn-sm">Cancel</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="section-card">
            <div class="section-header">Available Profiles</div>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-0 px-3 pt-3">Every Profile currently available for this Objective's proposed Capabilities, and which Template it belongs to — a Profile's own Template need not cover every Capability listed on its card; anything it doesn't, the Profile can add via Additional Capabilities.</p>
            <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 g-3 p-3">
              <% fromObjective.commissioningOptions.forEach(function(row) { %>
                <div class="col">
                  <label class="card-tile profile-tile d-flex gap-2 h-100 mb-0" for="tp-<%= row.templateId %>-<%= row.profile ? row.profile.id : 'none' %>" style="cursor: pointer;">
                    <input class="form-check-input mt-1 flex-shrink-0" type="radio" name="templateProfile" value="<%= row.templateId %>|<%= row.profile ? row.profile.id : '' %>" id="tp-<%= row.templateId %>-<%= row.profile ? row.profile.id : 'none' %>">
                    <span class="small">
                      <% if (row.profile) { %>
                        <span class="component-name"><%= row.profile.name %></span> <code class="text-muted small"><%= row.profile.code %></code> (<%= row.profile.environment %>)
                      <% } else { %>
                        <span class="component-name">No Profile yet</span> <span class="component-note">— a default will be created</span>
                      <% } %>
                      <div class="component-note">Template: <%= row.templateName %> <code class="text-muted"><%= row.templateCode %></code></div>
                      <% if (row.capabilities.length) { %>
                        <div class="component-note">Capabilities: <%= row.capabilities.map(function(c) { return c.label; }).join(', ') %></div>
                      <% } %>
                    </span>
                  </label>
                </div>
              <% }) %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </form>
      <% } %>
    <% } else { %>
    <%# Redesigned (owner, 2026-09-06: "the SEU is commissioned against an
         objective... If the commissioning happens from SEU, then Objective
         also has to be picked") — replaces the old freeform statement +
         Capability-checklist form (which auto-created an Objective inline
         and auto-matched a Template, no real choice offered). An SEU is
         always commissioned against a real Objective, so starting from the
         SEU side now means picking one of those, same as arriving via the
         Objective's own "Commission SEU" action — both converge on this
         same route with ?objectiveId= set, and the identical Template/
         Profile tree above. %>
    <h2 class="h3 mb-1 text-dark fw-bold">Commission a new SEU</h2>
    <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Pick which Objective to commission against.</p>

    <% var objs = locals.commissionableObjectives || []; %>
    <% if (!objs.length) { %>
      <div class="alert alert-warning">
        No Objective is currently eligible to commission against (Active, non-Strategic, a leaf, not already commissioned). <a href="/aisworg/seu/objectives">Decompose and activate one first</a>.
      </div>
    <% } else { %>
      <%# CR-083 — aligned to the same .section-card/.component-row system
           as the picker above, replacing the plain Bootstrap card/list-group
           markup this used before. %>
      <div class="section-card">
        <div class="section-header">Eligible Objectives</div>
        <% objs.forEach(function(o) { %>
          <div class="component-row d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <span class="tier-badge"><%= o.tier %></span>
            <span class="flex-grow-1 small"><% if (o.displayId) { %><span class="display-id-pill me-1"><%= o.displayId %></span><% } %><%= o.statement %></span>
            <a href="/aisworg/seu/seus/new?objectiveId=<%= o.id %>" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary"><i class="bi bi-rocket-takeoff me-1"></i>Commission</a>
          </div>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
    <% } %>
    <% } %>
  </main>

  <%- include('../../partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
